note bce fixture shapes: erasure in a local array, an edit parameter, a const count, a bound, nested loops,
note break and continue, and a call of an inline function that writes its own copy of the counter.
note Exit, the same with and without bce: tri gives 36; then the loop with continue and break adds 63, the
note nested loops 224 and the inline loop 320: 643 mod 256 = 131 (Wolfram).
const N ulong 16
fn tri a edit ulong 8 to ulong
for i ulong 8
put a i add get a i i
end
t = ulong 0
for i ulong 8
t = add t get a i
end
ret t
end
fn bump x ulong to ulong inline
x = add x 5
ret x
end
fn main to int
v = new ulong 16 0
for i ulong N
put v i i
end
w = new ulong 8 1
s = tri w
for i ulong 16 bound 100
if eq i 3
continue
end
if eq i 12
break
end
s = add s get v i
end
m = new ulong 64 0
for i ulong 8
for j ulong 8
put m add mul i 8 j add i j
s = add s get v i
end
end
for i ulong 16
s = add s bump i
s = add s get v i
end
ret int rem s 256
end
